       ee22ssccrruubb [[OOPPTTIIOONN]] MMOOUUNNTTPPOOIINNTT || DDEEVVIICCEE

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ee22ssccrruubb  attempts  to  check (but not repair) all metadata in a mounted
       ext[234] file system if the file system resides on an LVM logical  vol‐
       ume.  The block device of the LVM logical volume can also be passed in.

       This  program  snapshots the volume and runs a file system check on the
       snapshot to look for corruption errors.  The LVM volume group must have
       at least 256MiB of unallocated space to dedicate to the snapshot or the
       logical volume will  be  skipped.   The  snapshot  will  be  named  _l_v_‐
       _n_a_m_e.e2scrub  and  uuddeevv  will  not  create  symbolic  links to it under
       _/_d_e_v_/_d_i_s_k.  Every attempt will be made to remove the snapshots prior to
       running  ee22ssccrruubb, but in a dire situation it may be necessary to remove
       the snapshot manually.

       If no errors are found, ffssttrriimm can be called on the file system  if  it
       is  mounted.   If  errors  are found, the file system will be marked as
       having errors.  The file system should be taken offline and ee22ffsscckk  run
       as  soon as possible, because ee22ssccrruubb does not fix corruptions.  If the
       file system is not repaired, ee22ffsscckk will be run before the next mount.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --nn     Print what commands ee22ssccrruubb would execute to check the file sys‐
              tem.   (Note:  the  commands will not actually be executed; how‐
              ever, since ee22ssccrruubb needs to run some commands to query the sys‐
              tem to determine what commands would be executed, it still needs
              to be run as root.)

       --rr     Remove the e2scrub snapshot and exit without checking anything.

       --tt     Run ffssttrriimm((11)) on the mounted file system if no errors are found.

       --VV     Print version information and exit.

